A||N||3||grinthock||Leaky O2?||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||12-02-2001||01:21 AM||||Looks like I might have found my rich running problem.<P>Looked tonight when car was cold and noticed with a flashlight there was exhaust exiting around the O2 sensor from between the threads, any idea how I could "seal" it up?  O2 sensor IS good (althought probably fowled from all the rich running)<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||12-02-2001||02:42 AM||||I've never heard of an O2 sensor leaking through the threads...are you sure it's tightened all the way up and not cross-threaded???<P>If it is leaking out, it would still be very light...but I'll offer a way to do it regardless.<P>If you need to seal up the O2 bung, the best way I would propose is using Copper RTV silicone, laying a bead around the upper (closer to wire) 50% of the threads.  You can't get silicon into the "flow" part of the exhaust, as silicone poisoning ruins O2 sensors.  Another thing you may want to look for is a black tarry substance called "Accoustiseal"...available at good parts stores and some hot rod shops.  It seals anything exhaust about 5 times better than gaskets.<P>Really, this shouldn't be an issue, I'd check for tightness and cross-threading if it is leaking.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||12-02-2001||04:24 AM||||Hey Justin!<BR>The O2 sensor should have a gasket just like a spark plug...<BR>If yours is missing, then replace it with a spark plug gasket...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-02-2001||10:40 AM||||leaking around the threads would most likely be a bad/missing gasket or a cracked bung. make sure the bung weld or the manifold right by the bung hasn't cracked. <P>One thing you never do is seal the shell on the sensor...... the shell has to breath for the sensor to work. If the sensor is leaking out the shell then it's bad and needs replacement.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
